<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n77541" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πανσέληνος</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πασσ-</span></b>  (<i><span class="en">
			Arist.
			<u>APo.</u>
			93a37
		</span></i> cod. A), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, of the moon, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>at the full</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ σελήνη ἐτύγχανε οὖσα π.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					7.50
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κύκλος π.</span>
			<i>the moon's full</i> orb, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ion</u>
				1155
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰς νύκτας τὰς π.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>HA</u>
					622b27
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ πανσέληνος</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὥρα</span>) <i>the time of full moon</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.47
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				6.120
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				84
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰν αὔριον π.</span> (s. v.l.)
			at to-morrow's <i>full moon</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OT</u>
				1090
			</span></i> (lyr.): without the Art., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πανσέληνος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Th.</u>
					389
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				And.
				1.38
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταῖς πανσελήνοις</span> or
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν ταῖς π.</span>
			<i>at the seasons of full moon</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				544a20
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				555a10
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Stoic.</u>
				1.34
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πανσέληνον, τό</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Apollon.
				<u>Mir.</u>
				36
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>round as the full moon</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρυσίς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hermipp.
					37
				</span></i>
			 (dub. l.).</div>
